w, P is on AB, and E is on PD. Polygon ABCDEF, with dimensions in inches as marked, has an area of 122 square inches. What is the area of △PEB, in square inches?\n[Figure: polygon ABCDEF made of an upper rectangle (A top-left, F top-right; AF = 4, left side = 8) sitting on a lower rectangle (P–E–D–C–B with PE = 4, ED = 11, BC = 15); P is on left side AB; E is on segment PD. The lower rectangle's height PB is unknown; total area = 122, so 8·4 + 15·PB = 122, giving PB = 6.]", "choices": [{"key": "F", "text": "3 13/15"}, {"key": "G", "text": "6"}, {"key": "H", "text": "12"}, {"key": "J", "text": "13 11/13"}, {"key": "K", "text": "15"}], "correct": "H", "explanation": "Source-keyed answer from book_t4.md (T4-44)."}, "fields": {"stem": "Polygon ABCDEF has area 122 square inches. P lies on AB, and E lies on PD. APEF and PBCD are rectangles, with AP=8, AF=PE=4, ED=11, and BC=15 inches. What is the area of triangle PEB, in square inches?", "assets_patch": {"figure_required": false, "source_verification_date": "2026-09-29", "figure_reconstruction": "2026-09-29-from-explicit-givens", "reconstruction_basis": "Only geometry/labels explicitly present in the source transcription; no missing numeric data inferred.", "figure": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,"}}}, {"id": "d697f104-4982-5e37-afcd-8cdb41ec08c5", "source": "Existing complete source transcription T4-44; mathematical reconstruction, not a recovered original scan", "review_note": "Rebuilt a precise diagram from complete explicit givens. Independently verified the answer and each alternative; replaced source-key-only explanation.", "explanation": "The upper rectangle has area 8·4=32. The lower rectangle therefore has area 122−32=90 and width 15, so PB=90/15=6. Triangle PEB is right with perpendicular legs PE=4 and PB=6. Its area is (1/2)·4·6=12 square inches (H).", "correct": "H", "release": true, "before": {"stem": "In the figure below, P is on AB, and E is on PD. Polygon ABCDEF, with dimensions in inches as marked, has an area of 122 square inches. What is the area of △PEB, in square inches?\n[Figure: polygon ABCDEF made of an upper rectangle (A top-left, F top-right; AF = 4, left side = 8) sitting on a lower rectangle (P–E–D–C–B with PE = 4, ED = 11, BC = 15); P is on left side AB; E is on segment PD. The lower rectangle's height PB is unknown; total area = 122, so 8·4 + 15·PB = 122, giving PB = 6.]", "choices": [{"key": "F", "text": "3 13/15"}, {"key": "G", "text": "6"}, {"key": "H", "text": "12"}, {"key": "J", "text": "13 11/13"}, {"key": "K", "text": "15"}], "correct": "H", "explanation": "Source-keyed answer from book_t4.md (T4-44)."}, "fields": {"stem": "Polygon ABCDEF has area 122 square inches. P lies on AB, and E lies on PD. APEF and PBCD are rectangles, with AP=8, AF=PE=4, ED=11, and BC=15 inches. What is the area of triangle PEB, in square inches?", "assets_patch": {"figure_required": false, "source_verification_date": "2026-09-29", "figure_reconstruction": "2026-09-29-from-explicit-givens", "reconstruction_basis": "Only geometry/labels explicitly present in the source transcription; no missing numeric data inferred."}}, "figure_from_id": "70d61a5f-5630-5bda-ad5c-606d6aa1bc0b"}, {"id": "fefc225a-9f1b-56b5-903b-063c8e5d7fce", "source": "Existing complete source transcription T5-28; mathematical reconstruction, not a recovered original scan", "review_note": "Rebuilt a precise diagram from complete explicit givens. Independently verified the answer and each alternative; replaced source-key-only explanation.", "explanation": "F identifies congruent corresponding angles; H and J identify congruent alternate exterior angles; K identifies congruent alternate interior angles. Each has a converse proving parallel lines. G states that same-side exterior angles 1 and 7 are congruent; these must be supplementary for parallel lines and congruence alone is insufficient. Therefore G.", "correct": "G", "release": true, "before": {"stem": "In the plane shown in the figure below, lines m and 